  "title": "Black Hole Log",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "story": "The leak sensor dumps readings until it sends a `0`, and nobody knows how many there'll be: could be 3, could be thousands. Store them all and replay them **newest first**.\n\nInput: non-zero whole numbers separated by spaces, then a `0`.\n\nOutput: the readings in reverse order, one per line. If the `0` comes first, print `empty`.\n\nExample: `5 3 9 0` prints `9`, `3`, `5`.",
  "starter": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int log[100];\n    int count = 0, value;\n    while (scanf(\"%d\", &value) == 1 && value != 0) {\n        log[count++] = value;\n    }\n    // print them newest first\n    return 0;\n}\n",
